# Pairs with HandOffBound. Moved from the design's
# ReadPositionHonestRangeDeletePerShardClose. Each shard's walk is stamped with
# its own shard's routing generation, so the close holding L re-claims only its
# own. Another shard's walk, still in flight after its fan-out was abandoned, is
# never rejected and is allocated above the heads that close recorded.
MODULE: HandOffBoundRangeDeletePerShardClose
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: another shard's range-delete walk is not fenced by the close holding L
PERTURBS: GAlloc, GReject

--- FIND
    /\ gst \in {"pend", "repend"}
    /\ gstamp >= fFence
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- REPLACE
    /\ gst \in {"pend", "repend"}
\* MUTATION: stamped with its own shard's generation, which this close does not re-claim.
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ gst \in {"pend", "repend"}
    /\ gstamp < fFence
--- REPLACE
    /\ gst \in {"pend", "repend"}
\* MUTATION: this close never rejects it.
    /\ FALSE
--- END
